  "body": "**FREEHOLD RESOURCE CONSENT APPROVED - 639sqm CORNER SITE IN PREMIUM POSTCODE**\r\n\r\nResource consent has now been approved for the conversion from cross-lease to a 639sqm freehold corner title, adding a very compelling dimension to this Rothesay Bay property.\r\n\r\nIf you've been waiting for the right street in the Bays and a home that offers scope to create something truly special, this could be the one.\r\n\r\nSet in one of Rothesay Bay's sought-after streets, with the beach at the end of the road and premium homes nearby, this is your chance to secure a coastal address with a future worth imagining.\r\n\r\nWith a substantial brick exterior, tropical palms and unmistakable 1970s flair, the home has individuality from the outset. Inside, the character continues with a striking staircase, a raised ceiling with high-level windows, and sculptural brickwork featuring multiple arched display niches. This is serious retro chic with an identity all its own. Enjoy as is or start planning the make-over.\r\n\r\nFour double bedrooms, three bathrooms and two generous living areas provide room for everyone. With three bedrooms upstairs and one downstairs, there's flexibility for multi-generational living, teenagers or adult children wanting their own space. You'll love the spacious master suite, complete with a walk-in wardrobe and ensuite with a separate bath. A true retreat.\r\n\r\nThe outlook is breathtaking, with views towards Rangitoto and the Hauraki Gulf in one direction, and Whangaparaoa and Tiritiri Matangi in the other. From the lounge and kitchen, the scenery becomes part of everyday life, with doors opening onto a covered wraparound deck that extends the living space outdoors. Enjoy a morning coffee with a sunrise view, dine alfresco or head downstairs to the dedicated BBQ zone for relaxed entertaining.\r\n\r\nThere's substantial off-street parking, too, with room for the boat, motorhome and beach toys - a real bonus for coastal living.\r\n\r\nRothesay Bay and Churchill Cove are within walking distance, as is Murrays Bay Wharf, while local cafes and shops are approximately 300 metres away. Families will appreciate the school zones for Browns Bay Primary, Murrays Bay Intermediate, Northcross Intermediate and Rangitoto College.\r\n\r\nWith neighbouring homes demonstrating the appeal of this prestigious street, savvy buyers will recognise the chance to secure a premium position and imagine what the future could hold.\r\n\r\n**A premium postcode. A unique property. A future worth exploring.**",
